{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1784525339,"nonce":"qvwE1GwSxUdzPBeYQ0RCvQd5DIA=","title":"The Run-pipeline ref picker (`ui/scarab-web-ui/src/routes/RunPipeline.tsx`) is a","message":"free-text box: you must type an exact branch / tag / SHA before \"Load pipelines\"\ncan resolve it. There is no way to browse or search the repo's refs from the UI,\nso it's easy to fat-finger a branch name and get a bare \"could not read\npipelines at this ref\" with no discoverability.\n\nRoot cause: there is **no backend endpoint to enumerate refs**. Confirmed against\n`openapi.json` and `ui/scarab-web-ui/src/api/client.ts` — no `.../branches`,\n`.../tags`, or `.../refs` route exists. The forge adapters (GitHub / Forgejo,\nADR-0045/0046) can list refs, but nothing surfaces them.\n\n\n1. **Backend**: add `GET /v1/repos/{org}/{repo}/refs?q=\u003cquery\u003e` backed by the\n   ForgeConnection. Returns branches + tags (kind + name + short SHA). Scope v1\n   to branches+tags only; recent-commits / open-PR head-refs are a possible\n   follow-up, not part of this.\n2. **Frontend**: replace the free-text input with a combobox over that endpoint —\n   live-filtered dropdown, each row tagged branch/tag, still allowing a full SHA\n   typed directly to pin. Resolved short-SHA line stays below (as it is now,\n   after the recent layout fix).\n\n\n```\n BRANCH / TAG / SHA\n+----------------------------------------+\n| fea|                          [Load]   |\n+----------------------------------------+   \u003c- dropdown, filtered live\n| (branch)  feat/adr-0056-takes          |\n| (branch)  feat/runs-list-origin        |\n| (tag)     v0.3.1                        |\n| (tag)     v0.3.0                        |\n| ...type a full SHA to pin directly     |\n+----------------------------------------+\n   resolved 289b4ee\n```\n\n\n- Split out of a batch of Run-detail / Run-pipeline UI polish fixes (activity\n  panel surface, artifacts/logs empty-state insets, ref-SHA layout, secrets\n  modal + overwrite guard, and a Workspace-tab crash fix) — those were\n  CSS/component-only and landed together; this one is the only item that needs\n  new backend + a real forge, hence a separate ticket.\n- Wants a live-cluster verification since it exercises the forge adapters.","files":null}]}